  "reason": "The current best is config_039 (multimodal, multiprofile, scVI_n200, ViT-L, transformer, weighted) at 0.7250. The evidence strongly supports scVI_n200 as the best RNA encoder (outperforming PCA by ~0.04 and scGPT by ~0.14 in RNA-only), transformer aggregation over avgpool, weighted fusion over concat, and multiprofile over singleprofile. The only untested dimension within this optimal pipeline is the image encoder: ViT-L vs. ResNet50. While ResNet50 was very poor in isolation (0.2079 image-only), config_033 isolates whether a weaker image encoder in a weighted-fusion multimodal pipeline can still contribute or whether ViT-L's strength is essential. This is the most principled single-variable extension of the current best, keeping all other components at their validated optima. As the final experiment, it either confirms ViT-L's necessity or reveals a comparable alternative, maximizing information gain without compounding multiple uncertain changes."
}

